#### Overview

## How do you get a beginner from an idea to working hardware?

Incipe Academy teaches hardware to beginners. Incipe Workspace is its desktop app: describe what your hardware should do, and an AI agent plans the board, writes the firmware and shows every live connection in 3D. I designed and built it.

#### Problem

## One sensor took six steps before you could build anything.

Most beginners give up somewhere in this list, long before they reach their idea. And both paths still end in the same place: the application logic is the part they actually came to write.

{% flows outcome="Integrate, deploy & test" note="Application logic is needed either way." %}
{% flow title="Traditional setup" steps="Read datasheets & register maps | Wire & power the sensor | Install & integrate drivers | Write configuration & reading code | Calibrate & debug readings | Build data logging" /%}

{% flow title="Incipe" steps="Snap in the sensor | Read it with one line of code" /%}
{% /flows %}

#### Solution

## Incipe cuts it to two.

Snap the sensor into Incipe Board, then read it with one line of code using the Incipe libraries. Incipe Workspace mirrors every live connection on screen, so learners see the effect of each change the moment they make it.

